# Relationship-based authorization with the SISVendor and EdFiSandbox claim sets.
#
# - People (students, staff, contacts) can be created by anyone with the claim, but are only
#   readable once a relationship links them to one of the client's education organizations.
# - A collection query for an unrelated record returns 200 with an empty array; a GET by id
#   returns 403 ("Authorization Denied").
# - Education organizations are readable by everyone; only EdFiSandbox may create them.
#
# Credentials: the single-tenant review-variant applications (add-review-variants.ps1 output):
#   SISVendor District    - Grand Bend ISD 255901, namespace uri://ed-fi.org
#   SISVendor School      - Grand Bend school 255901107 only, namespace uri://ed-fi.org
#   EdFiSandbox District  - 255901, namespace uri://ed-fi.org (the broad "Sandbox" claim set)
# The same walkthrough works on /mt-dms/{tenant}/{schoolYear} with that tenant's variant keys.
# Re-running: creates return 201 the first time and 200 (upsert) after that.

@base = https://your-label.eastus.cloudapp.azure.com
@realm = edfi
@dms = {{base}}/st-dms

# The raw `Basic key:secret` form below is base64-encoded automatically by VS Code REST Client.
# Pre-encode it instead (`Authorization: Basic <base64(key:secret)>`) if a secret contains
# characters REST Client treats as variables ({{ }}) or your client does not auto-encode the raw form.
@districtKey = REPLACE_WITH_SISVENDOR_DISTRICT_KEY
@districtSecret = REPLACE_WITH_SISVENDOR_DISTRICT_SECRET
@schoolKey = REPLACE_WITH_SISVENDOR_SCHOOL_KEY
@schoolSecret = REPLACE_WITH_SISVENDOR_SCHOOL_SECRET
@sandboxKey = REPLACE_WITH_EDFISANDBOX_DISTRICT_KEY
@sandboxSecret = REPLACE_WITH_EDFISANDBOX_DISTRICT_SECRET

### Get a token for SISVendor District (255901)
# @name tokenRequestDistrict
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{districtKey}}:{{districtSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@district = {{tokenRequestDistrict.response.body.access_token}}

### Get a token for SISVendor School (255901107)
# @name tokenRequestSchool
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{schoolKey}}:{{schoolSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@school = {{tokenRequestSchool.response.body.access_token}}

### Get a token for EdFiSandbox District (255901)
# @name tokenRequestSandbox
POST {{base}}/auth/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token
Authorization: Basic {{sandboxKey}}:{{sandboxSecret}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials

###
@sandbox = {{tokenRequestSandbox.response.body.access_token}}

### Review what the district token is authorized to do: claim set, namespace prefixes, and the
# education organizations (with their descendants) it is bound to.
POST {{dms}}/oauth/token_info
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{district}}"
}

#
# Education Organizations
#

### Create a new school in LEA 255901 with SISVendor. DENIED (403): this claim set may only read schools.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": 255901998,
  "nameOfInstitution": "Security Review Middle School",
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": 255901 },
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade" }
  ]
}

### Same school with the EdFiSandbox claim set, which is not intended for production data. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{sandbox}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": 255901998,
  "nameOfInstitution": "Security Review Middle School",
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": 255901 },
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade" }
  ]
}

### SISVendor can read it. ALLOWED: schools are not personally identifiable, so every client may read them.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/schools?schoolId=255901998
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

### Create a new Local Education Agency OUTSIDE Grand Bend, with Sandbox credentials. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/localEducationAgencies
Authorization: Bearer {{sandbox}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "localEducationAgencyId": 255999,
  "nameOfInstitution": "Security Review Outside District",
  "localEducationAgencyCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/LocalEducationAgencyCategoryDescriptor#Independent",
  "categories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#Local Education Agency" }
  ]
}

### And a school in it. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/schools
Authorization: Bearer {{sandbox}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "schoolId": 255999001,
  "nameOfInstitution": "Security Review Outside School",
  "localEducationAgencyReference": { "localEducationAgencyId": 255999 },
  "educationOrganizationCategories": [
    { "educationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/EducationOrganizationCategoryDescriptor#School" }
  ],
  "gradeLevels": [
    { "gradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade" }
  ]
}

#
# Students and Enrollment
#

### Create a student with the district token. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1",
  "firstName": "Review",
  "lastSurname": "Student",
  "birthDate": "2010-01-01"
}

### Read the student back. There is no relationship yet: the request is allowed, but the array is EMPTY.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students?studentUniqueId=SR-STUDENT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

### Enroll the student in the school outside 255901's hierarchy. DENIED (403).
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/studentSchoolAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1" },
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": 255999001 },
  "entryDate": "2025-08-15",
  "entryGradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade"
}

### Enroll the student in a school that IS in 255901's hierarchy. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/studentSchoolAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1" },
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": 255901001 },
  "entryDate": "2025-08-15",
  "entryGradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade"
}

### Read the student again. ALLOWED: the record is returned.
# @name districtStudent
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students?studentUniqueId=SR-STUDENT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

### The Sandbox client is also bound to 255901, therefore ALLOWED.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students?studentUniqueId=SR-STUDENT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{sandbox}}

### The school-level client (255901107) has no relationship to a 255901001 student: EMPTY array.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students?studentUniqueId=SR-STUDENT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{school}}

### Same student by id with the school-level client. DENIED (403), with a hint to create a StudentSchoolAssociation.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/students/{{districtStudent.response.body.$[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{school}}

### The school-level client tries to enroll the student in a sibling school. DENIED (403).
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/studentSchoolAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{school}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1" },
  "schoolReference": { "schoolId": 255901044 },
  "entryDate": "2025-08-15",
  "entryGradeLevelDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/GradeLevelDescriptor#Ninth grade"
}

#
# Staff
#

### Create a staff member. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/staffs
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffUniqueId": "SR-STAFF-1",
  "firstName": "Review",
  "lastSurname": "Staff"
}

### Again, unable to read the staff member until there is a relationship: EMPTY array.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/staffs?staffUniqueId=SR-STAFF-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

### Establish a relationship. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/staffEducationOrganizationAssignmentAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "staffReference": { "staffUniqueId": "SR-STAFF-1" },
  "educationOrganizationReference": { "educationOrganizationId": 255901001 },
  "staffClassificationDescriptor": "uri://ed-fi.org/StaffClassificationDescriptor#Teacher",
  "beginDate": "2025-08-01"
}

### Read the staff member again. ALLOWED this time.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/staffs?staffUniqueId=SR-STAFF-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

#
# Contact (aka parent/guardian)
#

### Create a contact. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contactUniqueId": "SR-CONTACT-1",
  "firstName": "Review",
  "lastSurname": "Contact"
}

### Read the contact. Once again there is no relationship, therefore an EMPTY array.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/contacts?contactUniqueId=SR-CONTACT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}

### The school-level client cannot link the contact to a student it has no relationship with. DENIED (403).
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/studentContactAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{school}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1" },
  "contactReference": { "contactUniqueId": "SR-CONTACT-1" }
}

### Link the contact to the enrolled student with the district client. ALLOWED.
POST {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/studentContactAssociations
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "studentReference": { "studentUniqueId": "SR-STUDENT-1" },
  "contactReference": { "contactUniqueId": "SR-CONTACT-1" }
}

### Try again. ALLOWED: the contact is returned.
GET {{dms}}/data/ed-fi/contacts?contactUniqueId=SR-CONTACT-1
Authorization: Bearer {{district}}
